 "context": "<figure id=\"fig-ch37_03_05\"><span data-type=\"media\" id=\"fs-idp73632\" data-alt=\"When blood glucose levels fall, the pancreas secretes the hormone glucagon. Glucagon causes the liver to break down glycogen, releasing glucose into the blood. As a result, blood glucose levels rise. In response to high glucose levels, the pancreas releases insulin. In response to insulin, target cells take up glucose, and the liver converts glucose to glycogen. As a result, blood glucose levels fall.\">\n<img src=\"https://openstax.org/apps/archive/20241024.164013/resources/39271c97948bd7945fc9ac121abf908f85a4e4df\" data-media-type=\"image/png\" alt=\"When blood glucose levels fall, the pancreas secretes the hormone glucagon. Glucagon causes the liver to break down glycogen, releasing glucose into the blood. As a result, blood glucose levels rise. In response to high glucose levels, the pancreas releases insulin. In response to insulin, target cells take up glucose, and the liver converts glucose to glycogen. As a result, blood glucose levels fall.\" width=\"280\" height=\"296\">\n</span>\n</figure>",
 "stimulus_html": "",
 "questions": [
  {
   "id": 544283,
   "is_answer_order_important": true,
   "stimulus_html": "",
   "stem_html": "Pancreatic tumors may cause excess secretion of glucagon. Type I diabetes results from the failure of the pancreas to produce insulin. Evaluate the claims below to select the statement that correctly assesses impacts of both of these conditions.",
   "answers": [
    {
     "id": 1069801,
     "content_html": "A pancreatic tumor and Type 1 diabetes will have opposite effects on blood sugar levels."
    },
    {
     "id": 1069802,
     "content_html": "A pancreatic tumor and Type 1 diabetes can both cause hyperglycemia."
    },
    {
     "id": 1069803,
     "content_html": "A pancreatic tumor and Type 1 diabetes can both cause hypoglycemia."
    },
    {
     "id": 1069804,
     "content_html": "Both pancreatic tumors and Type 1 diabetes result in the inability of cells to take up glucose."
    }
   ],
